
# Never commit secrets — use AWS Secrets Manager + ExternalSecrets
*-secrets-patch.yaml
*-secrets.yaml
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
# Certificates too -- an origin cert is not secret, but it has no business
# in the repo and its private key must never be one paste away from a commit.
*.crt
*.csr
*.pem

# Terraform — never commit state (plaintext secrets), plans, or provider binaries
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
# `terraform plan -out=tfplan` writes a file with NO extension, so *.tfplan
# misses it. The plan file holds every resource attribute -- never commit it.
tfplan
# The escape hatch takes the AWS transfer credentials as input vars. Nothing
# writes a tfvars file today, but the moment someone does rather than retyping
# a secret, it is committable. Cheaper to exclude it before that happens.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
tfplan.*
crash.log
.claude